    ],
    "Description": "### Summary\n\n`Set-Cookie` parsing created additional cookies from unrecognised `name=value` attributes, and `CookieJar` had no limit on the number of cookies stored or sent. A server could make the client store a very large number of cookies and generate very large `Cookie` headers.\n\n### Impact\n\nA malicious server could cause excessive memory and CPU use in a client, repeated on every redirect, and cause later requests to the same domain to build an excessively large `Cookie` header.\n\n---\n\nPatch: https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/6963ee0befec1502b6bb7b4db6c72d044c08f4fa",
